body:
Ok, returning to the MRP on 4.7 beta1, this bug only happens in the editor. HDR works as intended when you run the MRP as a game either running in the editor (embedded or not). This has not changed from dev5. I also managed to export the MRP to two different Linux executables with X11 and Wayland versions As expected, the Wayland executable opens with HDR working, and the X11 executable opens in SDR.

Also, on KDE Plasma, setting one of the Display Configurations settings in System Settings causes HDR to enable on the editor window when you focus the mouse onto the window and a visual part of the editor changes, like the mouse hovering over a button.

@allenwp Good to know the bug isn't an Nvidia Linux moment at least.
